cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the curated data workflow, please cite the associated manuscript and this repository."
title: "DOPO-EP-ML"
type: software
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-09-19

authors:
  - family-names: "Huang"
    given-names: "Xueling"

repository-code: "https://github.com/huangxueling027/DOPO-EP-ML"

license: MIT

abstract: >
  Reproducible machine-learning workflow for DOPO-derived flame-retardant
  epoxy systems, including literature-derived data standardization,
  structure–formulation modeling, grouped nested validation, model
  interpretation, applicability-domain analysis, independent literature-based
  external validation, and multi-objective virtual screening.

keywords:
  - DOPO
  - epoxy resin
  - flame retardant
  - machine learning
  - applicability domain
  - virtual screening
  - SHAP
